setrow('rq2.crown.units.open', '4', 'pending', J + 'Units neither delivered, decided Owning, justified nor unjoinable (= rq2.crown.units.gap 5 - decided-only 1): quadtree_bounds.nw and .se (field slots raw, no field-transaction row), quadtree_bounds_free::bounds#1 and quadtree_point_free::point#1 (slots raw; degraded kind-raw; code-generator hold box-param-caller-retains:<caller>:not-a-local, box_param.rs:1830/1877/1965). Check: delivered 55 + decided-only 1 + justified 1 + unjoinable 0 + open 4 = 61.', 'n/a', 'count')
setrow('rq2.crown.units.borrow-on-raw', '4', 'pending', FR + 'The table row "Borrow where the artifact holds raw ... preservation controls, not credits" (appendix/E.tex:136-137): the four named preservation controls of the 09-07 design section 2.2 (X rows), all re-verified in the frame\'s emitted trees as a borrow where CROWN\'s output holds the pointer raw: avl height::N, getBalance::N, preOrder::root; bst inorder::root. The design claims "no broader exhaustive count" (section 2.2). ALTERNATIVE, the seat\'s or the user\'s choice: an exhaustive count on the five programs with CROWN units = 46 (avl 5, bst 4, buffer 13, ht 8, quadtree 16; depth 0, layer 0, not synthetic, not byref; rq2_pos_counter key of fan-out 031; CROWN side calibrated 2,414 -> 1,711), list agents/artifacts/2026-10-06-analysis-fanout-082/s14/borrow-on-crown-raw.tsv; over the twenty the same join gives 2,775 of 6,108 (RQ2\'s rate comparison in another form, not a ledger row).', 'delivered', 'count')
for k in ['rq2.crown.units.delivered', 'rq2.crown.units.unjoinable', 'rq2.crown.units.ceiling', 'rq2.crown.units.gap']:
    replace_in(k, '57 subjects + 4 owning fields', '54 subjects + 7 fields: avl 8+2, bst 5+2, buffer 28, ht 2, quadtree 11+3 (corrected in analysis-fanout 082)')
replace_in('rq2.crown.units.delivered', 'Units delivered in CROWN\'s form: 52', 'Units delivered in CROWN\'s form (55 = 51 subjects + 4 fields, the avl and bst left / right): 52')
replace_in('rq2.crown.units.gap', 'quadtree\'s five (quadtree_bounds.nw / .se and quadtree.root fields with no row; quadtree_node_free::node and quadtree_point_free::point degraded unchanged; quadtree_bounds_free::bounds is the justified one).',
           'quadtree\'s five (CORRECTED in analysis-fanout 082): quadtree_bounds.nw and .se (fields, no row), quadtree_bounds_free::bounds and quadtree_point_free::point (degraded, model Raw), quadtree_node_free::node (degraded, model Owning = rq2.crown.units.decided-only); quadtree.root is the justified unit (C50), not bounds_free::bounds as 077 wrote. gap = decided-only 1 + open 4.')
